  "body_html": "<h1>Lattice Function</h1>\n<p>Let \\(V\\) be a right \\(D\\)-vector space. A lattice function on \\(V\\) assigns to\neach real number \\(s\\) an \\(o_D\\)-lattice \\(L_s\\), decreasing in \\(s\\),\ncompatible with scalar translation, and left-continuous:\n\\[\nL_t\\subseteq L_s\\quad(s&lt;t),\\qquad\nL_{s+\\nu(d)}=L_s d,\\qquad\nL_s=\\bigcap_{t&lt;s}L_t.\n\\]\nWrite\n\\[\nL_{r+}=\\bigcup_{t&gt;r}L_t,\\qquad\n\\operatorname{Jump}(L)=\\{r\\in\\mathbb R:L_r\\ne L_{r+}\\}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>The lattice function induces filtrations on \\(\\operatorname{End}_D(V)\\) and\n\\(\\operatorname{GL}_D(V)\\) by requiring an operator or group element to shift\neach \\(L_s\\) into \\(L_{s+r}\\).</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
